  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you're stuck without internet. On our side your laptop shows as offline, so it isn't getting out to the internet at all. Please try these steps in order and tell me what happens:\n\n1. Do your other devices on the same home Wi-Fi (phone, tablet, TV) load websites? If none of them do, the problem is your home network, not the laptop.\n2. Turn Wi-Fi off and back on, or forget your home network and reconnect to it.\n3. Restart your laptop.\n4. Restart your home router: unplug it, wait 30 seconds, plug it back in and give it a few minutes to come back up.\n5. If it still won't work, connect your laptop to your phone's hotspot or plug in a network cable. That tells us whether the laptop itself is working.\n\nOnce you're back online, please leave the laptop on and signed in for about 30 minutes so it can download updates. It hasn't done that for a while. Let me know how the steps go, especially step 1 and step 5, and we'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), working from home. Account active, not blocked, vpn_access true, no failed logins. Device BL-LT-0107 (Win11) is offline. Last check-in was 2026-09-29, and there's a warning: no check-in for 12 days (KB-018 threshold is over 7 days). Offline status fits KB-014: the laptop has no internet path. Sent the user the KB-014 quick check (do other devices work?) and fix steps (Wi-Fi toggle, restart laptop, restart router, hotspot/wired test). Also asked her to stay online for 30 minutes so the management agent checks in (KB-018). Next steps: if other devices also fail, it's her home ISP/router. If the laptop fails on a hotspot or wired connection too, escalate as a laptop hardware/OS network fault. Once she's connected, re-run check_device_status to confirm a fresh check-in. If it's online but still not checking in after a restart, escalate per KB-018. No security concerns found.",
